# Secrets must never enter a build context.
#
# A bare `.env` matches ONLY the root-level file — not `.env.production`, and not
# `docker/dev/.env`. Since every production Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, those two
# files were being baked into readable image layers along with ~27 credentials.
# The glob below matches all of them; the negation keeps the checked-in templates.
.env*
!.env*.example

*.log
